consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.06175601037913192,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":15.3,"_gate_rev_durability":0.0751999826284595,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":62.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.038869522088632716,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":54.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0019549775557780036,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":52.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.003668690915920616,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":93.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.15295,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.6,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":60.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Parke Bancorp, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Parke Bank that provides personal and business financial services to individuals and small to mid-sized businesses. Its accepts various deposit products, including checking, savings, money market, time, and other traditional deposit services, as well as individual retirement accounts and certificates of deposit. The company's loan portfolio consists of residential, commercial real estate, construction, commercial and industry, and consumer loans. It also offers debit cards, internet banking, and online bill payment services. Parke Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1999 and is headquartered in Washington Township, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Vito S. Pantilione | President, CEO & Director | Age 73 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 103 people. Revenue per employee of $775K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $378K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Parke Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $384M market cap on $80M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 8% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $39M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 49 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.05\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 33% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 61% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Parke Bancorp (NASDAQ:PKBK) CFO Jonathan Hill Sells 454 Shares of Company Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/parke-bancorp-nasdaqpkbk-cfo-jonathan-hill-sells-454-shares-of-company-stock.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793967782.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.883,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Critical Survey: Parke Bancorp (PKBK) and The Competition","source":"thelinco